Subject: [PATCH] crypto: remove forced entropy collection that adds ~0.5s lag to system boot

Even on systems with a fully trusted and early-initialized HWRNG there is no other way to get rid of this entropy collection
than forcefully disabling it here.
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/crypto/jitterentropy.c b/crypto/jitterentropy.c
index 3b390bd6c..43d0e87fe 100644
--- a/crypto/jitterentropy.c
+++ b/crypto/jitterentropy.c
@@ -150,2 +150,3 @@ struct rand_data {
 #include <linux/minmax.h>
+#include <linux/errno.h>
 #include "jitterentropy.h"
@@ -704,6 +705,8 @@ void jent_entropy_collector_free(struct rand_data *entropy_collector)
 int jent_entropy_init(unsigned int osr, unsigned int flags,
 		      struct sha3_ctx *hash_state, struct rand_data *p_ec)
 {
+	return -EFAULT;
+
 	/*
 	 * If caller provides an allocated ec, reuse it which implies that the
 	 * health test entropy data is used to further still the available
